## Hook intent (manual parity)

AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE hooks resolve via git root → `$root/.claude/hooks/…` and **will not fire** from AGENT-PLAYGROUND alone. Emulate their intent:

| Lifecycle      | Hooks (concept)                                                                              | Agent behavior                                                            |
| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Prompt intake  | quality-gate, optimizer, pipeline-context, context-budget, RAG freshness, rate-limiter reset | Refuse gate/severity bypass; inject pipeline context; watch context size  |
| Pre write/edit | prompt-write-guard, prompt-gate-enforcer                                                     | Don’t write when a quality gate is pending                                |
| Pre shell      | rate-limiter, branch/commit guards, shell-syntax, line-encoding                              | PowerShell on Windows; the platform shell on macOS/Linux; no force-push main; valid branch/commit patterns |
| Post write     | rag-index-sync                                                                               | Note stale RAG when AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE docs change; offer `/rag-sync` flow |
| Post shell     | harness-error-boundary                                                                       | Surface command failures; don’t silently continue past hard errors        |

To **execute** a hook script against AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE state (when useful), run this from the workspace root. The same `.py` invocation applies on Windows, macOS, and Linux:

```text
uv run ../AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE/.claude/hooks/<name>.py
```

(Many hooks expect Claude Code JSON on stdin — if invocation fails without that payload, apply the rule text instead of forcing a run.)

## MCP & tools

- Prefer AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE MCP servers (`workspace-knowledge`, `agent-memory`) when available in the session for retrieval/memory.
- If MCP is unavailable, fall back to Read/Grep under the AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE mount paths.
- Do not invent alternate MCP server layouts. The checked-in manifest is `.mcp.json.example`, a template to copy to `.mcp.json` locally (`.mcp.json` is not in this checkout). It defines `workspace-knowledge` and `agent-memory`, both under `core-component-00/platform/model-context-protocol-servers/`.

## Write boundaries

- Default new artifacts to **AGENT-PLAYGROUND**.
- Do not modify `AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE/.claude/` or AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE hook state unless the user explicitly requests AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE config changes.
- When playground work must follow AGENT-GLOBAL-BASE conventions (naming, pipeline docs, profiles), mirror those conventions locally.
